                     section("Representation and semantics", "The view stores const Matrix* and snapshots N=min(rows,columns). Direction defaults to directed_t; Index defaults to u32. All N vertices exist; a nonzero entry is an edge and its matrix value is the const edge property. Vertex/graph properties are empty markers. Edge IDs use row*N+column and edge_slots is N².",
                             "An undirected view enumerates only the upper triangle but row/column queries still read actual matrix entries. A symmetric matrix is therefore required for a coherent undirected interpretation. A zero-weight edge cannot be distinguished from absence. Unlike owning undirected graphs, loop degree is counted once by the view's scans. Index multiplication/representability is not explicitly guarded.",
                             "Public vertex_range, edge_reference/edge_range, neighbor_range, and incident_range borrow the view and matrix. Their returned iterator classes are private implementation types. as_graph_view creates the adapter."),
                     section("Complexity and invalidation", "Construction and pair lookup are O(1), edge count/enumeration O(N²), and degrees/neighborhoods O(N). Storage is O(1) beyond the matrix. Matrix replacement/destruction invalidates access; resizing also makes the cached dimension stale. Neither graph nor matrix storage is owned or copied."),
