                     section("Traversal behavior", "bfs marks discovery before queueing and records breadth-first parent/depth values. dfs uses an explicit stack with enter/finish phases, pushing incident edges in enumeration order and therefore processing siblings in reverse stack order. Both set the source's parent to itself. contains validates the descriptor sentinel, array bound, and reached flag.",
                             "A visitor can provide discover_vertex, examine_edge, and finish_vertex hooks; bool-like false discovery/examination stops work with status ok. null_visitor provides no hooks. Finish return values are ignored. BFS examines outgoing edges in a separate pass before enumerating out_neighbors; DFS examines scheduled incoming edges before discarding already discovered vertices. Neither result has a complete flag.",
                             "reachable performs a full BFS and tests the reached flag. diffusion also performs a full BFS, then truncates only order to the requested depth: parent, depth, and reached still describe vertices beyond the radius. random_walk returns the start plus at most steps selected neighbors, stops at a sink, and uses rng()%degree, with possible modulo bias."),
